# Tool shell integrations: hooks a tool installs into the shell itself, as
# opposed to the plain environment variables in ~/.zsh/environment.
#
# Sourced LAST from ~/.zshrc. A hook like direnv's has to be installed after
# anything that manipulates the prompt or precmd_functions, ~/.localrc
# included. The exception is an integration that adds to fpath: those have to
# run before compinit and belong up beside the completion sourcing instead.
#
# Guard each block on the tool being present, and use `if` rather than
# `cmd && eval`. With `&&`, a missing tool leaves $? at 1, which is harmless
# but shows as a phantom error in any prompt that displays the last exit code.

# direnv: auto-load and unload per-directory .envrc files.
if command -v direnv >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  eval "$(direnv hook zsh)"
fi
